      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "If we let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡x{sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
